      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`sendall` keeps the recipients that were given without an amount as the strings the user passed (spend.cpp:1399). Later it finds their outputs by comparing against `EncodeDestination` of each output script (spend.cpp:1564), which for bech32 is the canonical lowercase form.\r\n\r\nAn address given in uppercase is valid bech32, and `validateaddress` and `sendtoaddress` accept it. In `sendall` it never matches, so its output keeps the placeholder amount of 0 and the call fails:\r\n\r\n```\r\nsendall '[\"BCRT1Q...\"]'\r\nerror code: -8\r\nSpecified output amount to bcrt1q... is below dust threshold.\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis stores the canonical encoding of those addresses instead, so the comparison doesn't depend on how the address was written. Invalid addresses are still rejected later when the transaction is constructed.\r\n\r\nThe new `sendall_uppercase_address` in `wallet_sendall.py` sweeps the wallet to the uppercase form of an address. It fails on master with the dust error above and passes with the fix. `wallet_send.py` still passes.\r\n\r\n",
