      ],
      "message": "wallet: accept uppercase addresses without amount in sendall\n\nsendall remembers the recipients given without an amount as the strings\nthe user passed, and later finds their outputs by comparing against\nEncodeDestination of each output script, which is the canonical\nlowercase form for bech32. An address given in uppercase, which is\nvalid bech32 and accepted by the rest of the wallet, never matches. Its\noutput then keeps the placeholder amount of 0 and sendall fails with\n\"Specified output amount to bcrt1q... is below dust threshold.\"\n\nStore the canonical encoding of those addresses instead.",
